  <div class="document">

    <div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Even Hu'ezer</div>
    <div class="section-title">Eishus [Laws of Marriage] — §4</div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ HALACHIC RULING ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="halachic-ruling">
      <span class="hebrew">כֹּהֲנִים וּלְוִיִּים וְיִשְׂרָאֵל מֻתָּרִים לָבוֹא זֶה בָּזֶה וְהַוָּלָד הוֹלֵךְ אַחַר הַזָּכָר</span>
      <em>Kohanim</em>, <em>Leviim</em>, and <em>Yisraelim</em> are permitted to marry among one another, and the child follows the father.
    </div>

    <p>This ruling derives from the Mishnah, <em>Kidushin</em>, chapter 3. The text of that Mishnah is: "Wherever there is valid <em class="trans">kidushin</em> [betrothal] and no transgression, <b>the child follows the father</b>. Which case is this? A <em>Kohenes</em>, a <em>Leviyah</em>, and a <em>Yisraelis</em>, etc. And wherever there is valid <em>kidushin</em> and there is a transgression, <b>the child follows the deficient one</b>, etc."</p>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS ALEPH ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 1 — Joy in <em>Mitzvos</em>: Elevating Holiness through the Nine Chambers</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>This is elucidated through the Torah-teaching <em class="trans">"Emtza'isa d'Alma"</em> [<em>The Midpoint of the World</em>] in §24 — see there. The general principle [explained there] is that <b>through performing a <em>mitzvah</em> with joy, one elevates holiness from the <em class="trans">klippos</em> [husks/forces of impurity]</b> — in the aspect of <em class="trans">ketores</em> [incense]. And through this one merits to ascend higher and higher until one draws down the <span class="hl-yellow">blessings of the intellect</span> and rectifies <span class="hl-blue">the arranger and settler of the intellect</span>, which is the aspect of <em class="trans">Keser</em> [Crown]. And through this one merits attainment of the <span class="hl-green"><b>nine <em class="trans">heichalos</em> [chambers]</b></span> that are beyond [the realm of] souls, spirits, and higher souls — which are the aspect of attaining the light of the <em class="trans">Ein Sof</em> [Infinite One], in the aspect of <em class="trans">matay velo matay</em> [<em>reaching yet not reaching</em>]. The essential attainment [of these chambers] is through <span class="hl-orange">the pursuit of thought [<em class="trans">rdiyas hamachshavah</em>]</span> and through <span class="hl-pink">the restrainer [<em class="trans">hame'akev</em>]</span> — which is the arranger and settler — the aspect of <em>Keser</em>. All of this is rectified through performing <em>mitzvos</em> with joy. See there carefully.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>עַל-פִּי הַתּוֹרָה "אֶמְצָעִיתָא דְּעָלְמָא" בְּסִימָן כד, עַיֵּן שָׁם. וְהַכְּלָל שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי עֲשִׂיַּת הַמִּצְוָה בְּשִׂמְחָה, מַעֲלִין הַקְּדֻשָּׁה מֵהַקְּלִפּוֹת בִּבְחִינַת קְטֹרֶת, וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לַעֲלוֹת מַעְלָה מַעְלָה עַד שֶׁמַּמְשִׁיכִין בִּרְכוֹת הַשֵּכֶל וּמְתַקְּנִין הַמְסַדֵּר וְהַמְיַשֵּׁב שֶׁל הַשֵּכֶל, שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת כֶּתֶר וְכוּ', וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זוֹכִין לְהַשָּגַת תִּשְׁעָה הֵיכָלִין...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS BEIS ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 2 — The Purpose of Man; Husband and Wife as <em>Pursuit</em> and <em>Restraint</em></div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is <b>the essential purpose of a person who comes to this world</b> — namely, to come to know Him, may He be blessed — and this is achieved through the abovementioned principle: by performing <em>mitzvos</em> with joy, until one merits that his thought pursues attainment of the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em>, until he attains it in the abovementioned aspect through <span class="hl-orange">pursuit [<em class="trans">redifahs hamachshavah</em>]</span> and <span class="hl-pink">the restrainer [<em class="trans">hame'akev</em>]</span> — through which comes the essential attainment of the pristine lights mentioned above, which are the ultimate knowledge, the ultimate eternal good. Blessed is the one who merits this.</p>

      <p>And this is the essential <em>mitzvah</em> <b>to bring forth children into the world — in order to draw down the intellect-lights from generation to generation</b>, for the child's intellectual capacity [<em class="trans">moach</em>] derives from the father's, so that he may merit that his mind pursues attainment of the pristine lights mentioned above. And since these lights cannot be attained except through pursuit and restraint, therefore offspring cannot be drawn forth except through the <span class="hl-blue">union of man and woman</span>, as it is written:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">לֹא טוֹב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂה לוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ</span><br>"It is not good for man to be alone — I will make him a helper corresponding to him" [<em>Bereishis</em> 2:18].</span>

      <p>For man and woman flow in their supernal root from the two aspects mentioned — <span class="hl-orange">pursuit</span> and <span class="hl-pink">restraint</span>. The man is in the aspect of the [driving of] intellectual light [<em class="trans">moichin</em>], while the woman is drawn from the aspect of <span class="hl-pink"><em class="trans">tzimtzum</em> [contraction] and <em>din</em> [strict judgment]</span> — as is known, this flows in its root from the aspect of the restrainer mentioned above. For even though in its supernal root the restrainer is pure light — for it is the arranger and settler of the intellect — nevertheless since it is the aspect of restraining the intellect-lights, the aspect of <em>tzimtzum</em> flows from it, through which the woman's hold takes root, as is known. And therefore below, <span class="hl-pink">the forces of strict judgment take greater hold in her</span>, and from there the hold of the <em class="trans">klippos</em> and the <em>sitra achara</em> extends to take hold of her more — because she is drawn from the aspect of <em>tzimtzum</em> of the intellect-lights, through which the hold of the forces of judgment is known. But <em>above</em>, in her root, she flows from an exceedingly lofty aspect — namely the aspect of the arranger and settler of the intellect, which is the aspect of <em>Keser</em>.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">אֵשֶׁת חַיִל עֲטֶרֶת בַּעְלָהּ</span><br>"A woman of valor is the crown of her husband" [<em>Mishlei</em> 12:4]</span> — <em class="trans">"ateres"</em> [crown] specifically — the aspect of <em>Keser</em> as above. For no attainment is possible, and in particular the "birthing" of intellectual light, except through rectifying the arranger and settler as above. And since these lights cannot be attained except by entering the <span class="hl-orange"><em class="trans">heichalei hatemuros</em> [chambers of exchange/transformation]</span> — the place of the <em>klippos</em> — in order to elevate holiness from there in the aspect of <em>ketores</em>, etc., as is explained in that Torah-teaching on the saying of our Sages <em>"Omru leyay, mi yeimar?"</em> [<em>"They said to him, 'Who can say?'"</em>] — see there — therefore there lies the primary battle and trial in the matter of this desire.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of <b>the great obligation to gladden the bride and groom</b>, as our Sages of blessed memory said. And this is the aspect of what our Sages said: <em>"One who has no children should gladden his wife with a matter of <em>mitzvah</em>."</em> For the essential elevation of holiness from the <em>klippos</em> is through joy — through which one merits to attain the lights mentioned above, through the rectification of pursuit and restraint from which flow the roots of man and woman, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה עִקַּר הַתַּכְלִית שֶׁל הָאָדָם שֶׁבָּא לָעוֹלָם הַזֶּה בִּשְׁבִיל זֶה כְּדֵי לְהַכִּיר אוֹתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ... וְזֶה עִקַּר הַמִּצְוָה לְהַעֲמִיד בָּנִים בָּעוֹלָם כְּדֵי לְהַמְשִׁיךְ הַמֹּחִין מִדּוֹר לְדוֹר...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS GIMEL ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 3 — <em>Kohen</em>, <em>Levi</em>, and <em>Yisrael</em> as the Chain of Holiness</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>Kohen</em>, <em>Levi</em>, and <em>Yisrael</em> — who are the chain of holiness. The primary one is the <em>Kohen</em>, who is more sanctified than all Israel, for the <em>Kohen</em> was occupied with the service of the sacrifices and <em>ketores</em> — through which the holiness is refined from the <em>klippos</em> and rises higher and higher until one merits the blessings described there, which are the aspect of <span class="hl-yellow"><em class="trans">Birkas Kohanim</em></span> [the Priestly Blessing] — the aspect of: <em>"Vayisa Aharon es yadav el ha'am vayevarchem"</em> [<em>"And Aharon lifted his hands toward the people and blessed them"</em>] — which is the blessing of the intellect. And then the intellect-lights pursue [attainment of] the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em>.</p>

      <p>But it is also necessary that the <em>Levi</em> attach himself to [the Kohen] to serve him — for the essential rectification of the restrainer mentioned above is through the aspect of the <em>Levi</em>, who is the aspect of <span class="hl-pink"><em>tzimtzum</em> and judgment [<em>din</em>]</span> — as is known; he is the aspect of the restrainer. Therefore the <em>Levi</em> was occupied with <b>song</b> during the Temple service — for <em>"shir missmola"</em> — <em>"song is from the left"</em>, as stated in the holy Zohar. The left is the aspect of <em>tzimtzum</em> — the aspect of the restrainer. And this is the aspect of: <em>"ve'avad haLevi hu"</em> [<em>"and the Levi shall serve"</em>] — which is the aspect of <em>Keser</em>, as is understood from the holy Zohar — for the <em>Levi</em> corresponds to the restrainer, which is the aspect of <em>Keser</em>.</p>

      <p>And since the essential rectification mentioned above is through joy in <em>mitzvos</em>, therefore the <em>Yisraelim</em> stood at their post and were occupied with Torah during the Temple service — for Torah is the aspect of joy, as it is written:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">פִּקּוּדֵי ה' יְשָׁרִים מְשַׂמְּחֵי לֵב</span><br>"The precepts of Hashem are upright, gladdening the heart" [<em>Tehillim</em> 19:9].</span>

      <p>Through this comes the essential elevation of holiness from the <em>klippos</em> — which is the essential rectification of the sacrificial service conducted by the <em>Kohen</em>, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה בְּחִינַת כֹּהֵן, לֵוִי וְיִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁהֵם חֶבֶל הַקְּדֻשָּׁה... כִּי הָעִקָּר הוּא הַכֹּהֵן שֶׁהוּא מְקֻדָּשׁ מִכָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS DALET ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 4 — Why <em>Kohen</em>, <em>Levi</em>, and <em>Yisrael</em> May Intermarry; Why the Child Follows the Father</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>Therefore, <em>Kohanim</em>, <em>Leviim</em>, and <em>Yisraelim</em> are included within and bound to one another — and each one needs the other — for specifically through all three together the chain of holiness is completed, and one merits attainment of the lights mentioned above, as above. And therefore <span class="hl-blue"><em>Kohanim</em>, <em>Leviim</em>, and <em>Yisraelim</em> are permitted to intermarry</span>, for the holy union of man and woman — which in its root is the aspect of the totality of pursuit and restraint to attain the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> as above, which one merits through holy joy, the aspect of the joy of bride and groom as above — this itself is the aspect of the totality of <em>Kohen</em>, <em>Levi</em>, and <em>Yisrael</em>. For the <em>Kohen</em> corresponds to the <em>pursuit</em> of the intellect-lights — the aspect of the blessing of intellect; the <em>Levi</em> corresponds to the <em>restrainer</em>; and the <em>Yisrael</em> corresponds to the joy of Torah and <em>mitzvos</em>, as above. All are included together during the Temple service, through which the attainment of the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> is drawn — from which come the "births" of intellect-lights, from which come all births of holiness, as above.</p>

      <p>And therefore <b>the child follows the father</b> — for even though the woman's fear of Hashem is exceedingly lofty in its root — since she is drawn from the aspect of <em>Keser</em>, the aspect of <em>"eshes chayil ateres ba'alah"</em> as above — nevertheless the essential birth is the birth of intellect-lights to reveal knowledge of G-dliness in the world, which is drawn through the male specifically, who is in the aspect of the <em>pursuit</em> of intellect-lights. Therefore the child follows after him.</p>

      <p>All this applies where there is valid betrothal and no transgression — for when there is no transgression in the union, even if not everyone merits to sanctify himself so much that through his union he attains the lights mentioned above — nonetheless, since there is at least no transgression in his union, everything can be rectified through the offspring he produces, thereby fulfilling a <em>mitzvah</em> of the Torah. For through the birth of children from generation to generation, intellect-lights are drawn in each and every generation, until the children can merit attainment of the lights mentioned above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְעַל-כֵּן כֹּהֲנִים, לְוִיִּים וְיִשְׂרְאֵלִים כְּלוּלִים וּמְקֻשָּׁרִים זֶה בָּזֶה, וְכָל אֶחָד צָרִיךְ לַחֲבֵרוֹ...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS HEY ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 5 — When There Is Transgression: The Child Follows the Deficient One</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>But <b>when there is transgression, the child follows the deficient one</b> — for the moment there is an actual transgression in the union, the <span class="hl-pink"><em class="trans">heichalei hatemuros</em> [chambers of transformation/exchange]</span> overpower — for from there the arousal of the union originates, since one must enter there to refine holiness from within — and because of this there is a great battle in this matter. But when there is no transgression, the power of the <em>mitzvah</em> — which Hashem commanded to produce children — prevails, and holy intellect-lights are drawn through the birth; and then the child follows the male through whom flows the essential drawing of intellect-lights, as above. But when there is transgression, the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> overpower and draw the child after the deficient one — for they are ever lying in ambush for this, to draw deficiency, G-d forbid. May Hashem, blessed be He, save us.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>אֲבָל כְּשֶׁיֵּשׁ עֲבֵרָה אָז הַוָּלָד הוֹלֵךְ אַחַר הַפָּגוּם...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS VAV ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 6 — <em>Kidushay Kesef</em> (Betrothal with Money); Wealth, Incense, and the Descent of Divine Blessing</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of <em class="trans">kidushay kesef</em> — <span class="hl-yellow"><b>betrothal through money/silver</b></span> — that a woman is betrothed through money/silver [<em class="trans">kesef</em>]. For money and wealth in their root are exceedingly lofty — as is understood from the words of our master, teacher, and <em>rebbe</em>, of blessed memory [Rebbe Nachman of Breslov] — for it flows in its root from the aspect mentioned above, from the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above that are generated through pursuit and restraint, as above. For everything stated in this Torah-teaching about ascending higher and higher until one merits attainment of the nine chambers mentioned above — all of this is the <span class="hl-blue">secret of the <em>kavanos</em> [mystical intentions] of prayer</span>.</p>

      <p>The general principle of the <em>kavanos</em> is the ascent of the worlds — that <em>Malchus</em> rises from the <em>klippos</em> and clothes <em>Netzach</em>, <em>Hod</em>, <em>Yesod</em>; and <em>Netzach</em>, <em>Hod</em>, <em>Yesod</em> rise to clothe <em>Chesed</em>, <em>Gevurah</em>, <em>Tiferes</em>, etc., as is explained in the <em>kavanos</em>. And the one who merits to occupy himself with this rectification — the perfection of his rectification is when he ascends higher and higher until his thought pursues attainment of the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em>, in the aspect of <em class="trans">ratzo vashov</em> [<em>running and returning</em>].</p>

      <p>And the essential rectification is through the <em>arranger and settler</em> — the restrainer of the intellect-lights in their pursuit — which is the aspect of <em>Keser</em>. For without this rectification, the pursuit would have no restrainer and [the intellect-light] would remain there, annihilating itself from existence. And Hashem desires the continued existence of the world — therefore the essential perfection is through pursuit and restraint, as above. And the essential completion of the rectification is when one merits to return and draw from there all the good divine bounties — which is the aspect of the <span class="hl-green">descent of divine bounty after prayer</span> at the recitation of <em>"Ashrei"</em> and <em>"U'va l'Tzion"</em>.</p>

      <p>For during the <em>Shmoneh Esray</em> prayer one merits the aspect of attaining the lights mentioned above — but it must be in the aspect of <em>ratzo vashov</em> as above — and when in the aspect of <em>shov</em> [return], one draws from there all the good bounties, from which flows all money and wealth.</p>

      <p>The essential channel through which the divine bounty can descend below is through the aspect of the restrainer — therefore there the light begins to take form. And even though there no form [<em class="trans">tziyur</em>] is applicable at all — nevertheless since it is the aspect of restrainer, the light begins to contract somewhat, until through this there is a power below for [the light] to be formed as actual divine bounty, until money and wealth is drawn from there.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">עֲטֶרֶת חֲכָמִים עָשְׁרָם</span><br>"The crown of the wise is their wealth" [<em>Mishlei</em> 14:24]</span> — for wealth is drawn from the aspect of <em class="trans">atara</em> [crown] — the aspect of <em>Keser</em>, which is the arranger, settler, and restrainer of the intellect-lights in their pursuit, as above. And specifically <em>"ateres chachamim"</em> — for specifically the true wise men who merit the intellect-lights mentioned above — these constitute essential true wisdom — whose minds pursue the attainments mentioned above — specifically with them does wealth come from the aspect of <em>Keser</em> and crown. For they draw wealth from there, from <em>Keser</em>, which is the restrainer through which the essential rectification of the intellect-lights comes, as above. But for others, wealth may sometimes be drawn from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>, which sometimes channel divine bounty to such people when they do not merit to rectify the rectifications mentioned above properly.</p>

      <p>Therefore the woman is betrothed through <em>kesef</em> [silver/money] — for <em>kesef</em>, which is the divine bounty of wealth, flows in its root from there, from the aspect of <em>Keser</em>, from which her root [flows], as above. And this is what our master, teacher, and <em>rebbe</em>, of blessed memory, wrote: that wealth is one aspect together with the woman, and it is her vitality, and through it children depend — as is explained in the Torah-teaching on the prohibition of theft. See there carefully.</p>

      <p>For wealth — which is the descent of divine bounty — is drawn below through the arranger and settler, through which the pursuit of intellect-lights is in the aspect of <em>ratzo vashov</em> — and through this one draws divine bounty from there, and it is formed so that it can descend below, as above. And there is the root of the woman's vitality — which flows from the aspect of <em>tzimtzum</em> whose root is from the restrainer, as above. And through this comes the essential birth of children, which are the "births" of intellect-lights, which — when they are included there — must be in the aspect of <em>ratzo vashov</em>, until one returns and draws the intellect-lights below — from which come the births of children that flow from the father's intellectual capacity [<em>moach</em>] — in order that they reveal G-dliness in the world from generation to generation:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">דּוֹר לְדוֹר יְשַׁבַּח מַעֲשֶׂיךָ</span><br>"Generation to generation shall praise Your deeds" [<em>Tehillim</em> 145:4].</span>

      <p>For since in their root they flow from a supremely lofty place — from the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above — therefore specifically they can make known and reveal G-dliness in the world. And this is: <em>"U'gevurosecha yagidu"</em> — <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">וּגְבוּרֹתֶיךָ יַגִּידוּ</span><br>"And Your mighty deeds they shall declare" [<em>Tehillim</em> 145:6]</span> — <em>"gevurosecha"</em> [Your mighty deeds] specifically — namely the aspect of the restrainer and arranger, which is the root of the holy <em>gevuros</em> [mighty forces] — through this specifically they praise, declare, and publicize G-dliness below to all who inhabit the world.</p>

      <p>And therefore <span class="hl-green"><em>ketores</em> brings wealth</em></span> — for the essential ascent of the worlds in the aspect mentioned above is through the aspect of <em>"ketores yissamach lev"</em> [<em>"incense gladdens the heart"</em>] as above — and therefore it brings wealth, for from there flows all wealth, which is the descent of divine bounty after the <em>Shmoneh Esray</em> prayer, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה בְּחִינַת קִדּוּשֵׁי כֶּסֶף שֶׁהָאִשָּׁה מִתְקַדֶּשֶׁת בְּכֶסֶף, כִּי הַמָּמוֹן וְהָעֲשִׁירוּת בְּשָׁרְשׁוֹ גָּבֹהַּ מְאֹד...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS ZAYIN ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 7 — The Golden Calf; the Tabernacle; Forbidden Inquiry at the Highest Levels</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the reason why they were commanded regarding the construction of the Tabernacle after the sin of the Golden Calf, and all the work of the Tabernacle was through wealth — gold, silver, copper, etc. For the essential sin of the Golden Calf came about through the overpowering of the <span class="hl-pink"><em>heichalei hatemuros</em></span> — which overpowered because they drew sustenance from the wealth, as it is written: <em>"v'dai zahav"</em> — <em>"because of the gold you bestowed upon them"</em> — and they overpowered to such an extent that they came to actual idol worship, which is the ultimate exchange, G-d have mercy — the aspect of <em>"heymir goy Elokim"</em> [<em>"Can a nation exchange its G-d?"</em>].</p>

      <p>All this flowed from the fact that the <em>yetzer hara</em> [evil inclination] incited them and planted in their minds the idea to investigate the matter of the attainments mentioned above and to comprehend them with their own understanding. And by this they damaged greatly, until they came to idol worship. For in truth, it is forbidden to investigate there at all — for <em>"lo misddavkin velo yad'in"</em> — <em>"they are not grasped and not known"</em> — and this is what our master, teacher, and <em>rebbe</em>, of blessed memory, was precise about in that Torah-teaching: that even there, <span class="hl-yellow">faith is required</span> — both in the aspect of the blessing of intellect, which is the aspect of the pursuit of intellect-lights, and in the aspect of the arranger and settler — that even there <em>emunah</em> [faith] is required in the aspect of wondrous trusting, as is explained there. For these lights cannot be attained except when faith is combined with intellect — and then specifically one can attain them in the aspect of <em>matay velo matay</em>. But it is forbidden to stand and investigate there — for <em>"bam'ufla mimcha al tidrosh"</em> — <em>"in that which is wondrous beyond you, do not seek"</em> — for <em>"lo misddavkin velo yad'in velos man d'kayma behu"</em> [<em>"they are not grasped, not known, and none can stand before them"</em>] — as is explained in the language of the holy Zohar cited there.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of the damage [the Israelites] caused initially before the Giving of the Torah, when they had no water — as it is written there: <em>"al nasosam es Hashem leimor, hayesh Hashem b'kirbeinu im ayin"</em> — <em>"for their testing of Hashem by saying: 'Is Hashem in our midst or not?'"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 17:7]. The holy Zohar states that their damage was that they investigated whether the aspect of <em class="trans">yesh</em> [being] is within them, or the aspect of <em class="trans">ayin</em> [nothingness/nothing] — see there. That is, as above — their essential damage was their desire to stand and comprehend the attainments mentioned above, which are composed of <em>yesh</em> and <em>ayin</em> together — but one cannot stand before them, for one attains nine chambers which appear as if they are the aspect of <em>yesh</em> since they are nine chambers — yet nonetheless <em>"lo misddavkin velo yad'in"</em> — which is the aspect of <em>ayin</em>. And one who has strong faith and does not enter to investigate this at all — he merits to delight in Hashem and behold the pleasantness of His splendor, specifically through this, through the pursuit of thought and the restrainer. Blessed is he.</p>

      <p>But the moment one desires to investigate this, one stumbles greatly — for one can come to separation [from G-d], G-d forbid — which comes through the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>, which are the <em>sitra achara</em> <em>"d'sharya b'chibura v'sayem bifiruda"</em> [<em>"which begins in connection and ends in separation"</em>] — namely, that it separates between <em>yesh</em> and <em>ayin</em> until they doubted: <em>"Is Hashem in our midst or not?"</em> For in truth, all is one — but it is impossible to comprehend or investigate this at all, as above.</p>

      <p>And therefore they came to this at the time when they needed water — which is the drawing down of divine bounty that flows from the attainments mentioned above. And since they saw that the divine bounty was delayed from descending to them, through this they entered into the aforementioned trial: the aspect of <em>"al nasosam es Hashem, hayesh... im ayin"</em>, as above.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of the sin of the Golden Calf — when they said: <em>"Ki zeh Moshe ha'ish lo yada'nu meh hayah lo"</em> — <em>"For this Moshe, the man — we do not know what happened to him"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 32:1]. They erred and said that Moshe had been gathered and remained above, having been absorbed into <em>ayin</em>. Therefore they said: <em>"Kum asay lanu Elokim"</em> — <em>"Arise, make us a G-d"</em> — from gold and wealth. For they wanted to draw upon themselves the aspect of the restrainer itself, since through it all divine bounties flow — and therefore they damaged and made a separation between the aspect of the restrainer (from which flows all wealth) and the aspect of pursuit — and they did not want their thoughts to pursue higher and higher to attain the attainments mentioned above in the aspect of <em>matay velo matay</em>. Rather they wanted G-dliness drawn upon them in the aspect of actual <em>yeshus</em> [being/substance]. And this was the error of all idol worshipers of prior generations — all arising from the desires of this world.</p>

      <p>For in order to ascend and be included in the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above, one must shatter all desires and elevate the holiness from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>. But they wanted to follow their desires and to separate the divine bounty of wealth — which is drawn through the restrainer — and make from it actual G-dliness, G-d forbid. Therefore they went to Aharon — since Aharon was suited for the Priesthood and all the service of sacrifices and <em>ketores</em> was through him — through which specifically one merits attainment of the nine chambers mentioned above, from which all divine bounties are drawn through the formation via the restrainer — but they damaged and wanted to create the separation through him specifically, G-d forbid.</p>

      <p>Therefore the essential rectification was through the construction of the Tabernacle from the wealth of Israel — and then specifically Aharon was consecrated into the Priesthood and was commanded regarding the sacrificial service and <em>ketores</em> — through which everything was rectified — for they returned the wealth to holiness, to its root above, and made from it a Tabernacle where Aharon served in the sacrificial service and <em>ketores</em>, through which he elevated holiness from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>, ascending higher and higher until attaining the lights mentioned above as they should be rectified in the aspect of <em>matay velo matay</em> — through which all the damages mentioned above were rectified, which were the opposite of this.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה שֶׁנִּצְטַוּוּ עַל מְלֶאכֶת הַמִּשְׁכָּן אַחַר מַעֲשֵׂה הָעֵגֶל...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS CHES ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 8 — Nadav and Avihu; the Necessity of Marriage for the <em>Kohen</em></div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And Nadav and Avihu — who were awesome <em>tzadikim</em> — nonetheless <b>they damaged in the opposite direction</b>: they wanted only to ascend higher and higher with no restrainer whatsoever, and therefore they offered <em>ketores</em> at a time that was not their own, and entered without permission. Their entire damage was that they did not rectify the restrainer — the arranger and settler. This is the aspect of <em>"b'karvasam lifnay Hashem vayamusu"</em> — <em>"in their drawing near before Hashem they died"</em> [<em>Vayikra</em> 16:1] — they drew too close, more than was fitting, since they did not rectify the arranger and settler. Therefore Aharon was warned: <em>"v'al yavo b'chol eis el hakodesh"</em> — <em>"and he shall not come at all times into the sanctuary"</em> [<em>Vayikra</em> 16:2].</p>

      <p>And therefore <b>their damage was because they had not married</b> — as is stated in the holy Zohar — for the woman flows from the aspect of the arranger and settler, as above. Therefore a <em>Kohen</em> must be married, as is stated in the Zohar — and in particular the <em>Kohen Gadol</em> [High Priest] on Yom Kippur, who was forbidden to conduct the service if he was not married. For it is impossible to rectify the arranger and settler except when one is married to a woman — who flows from there, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְנָדָב וַאֲבִיהוּא שֶׁהָיוּ צַדִּיקִים נוֹרָאִים, אֲבָל הֵם פָּגְמוּ לְהֵפֶךְ...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS TES ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 9 — "Who Is Rich? One Who Is Happy with His Portion" — Hilchos Kesuvos</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>"Ezehu ashir? Hassamayach b'chelko"</em> — <b>"Who is rich? One who is happy with his portion"</b> [<em>Avos</em> 4:1] — for the essential rectification of wealth in holiness is through <span class="hl-yellow">joy specifically</span>. For specifically through joy one elevates holiness from the <em>klippos</em> until one merits to ascend and make all the rectifications mentioned above, until attaining the lights mentioned above through the aspect of pursuit and restraint — from which flows the descent of divine bounty, which is the aspect of wealth, as above.</p>

      <div class="sub-title">Hilchos Kesuvos [Laws of the Marriage Document]</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה בְּחִינַת אֵיזֶהוּ עָשִׁיר הַשָּמֵחַ בְּחֶלְקוֹ...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS YUD ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 10 — The Obligation of <em>Kesuvah</em>; Elevating the Wife; <em>Ratzo vaShov</em></div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of what one is obligated to give his wife a <em class="trans">kesuvah</em> [marriage contract], and it is forbidden to cohabit with one's wife without a <em>kesuvah</em>. For one is compelled to draw to her the divine bounty of wealth — through which comes the essential bond and connection between them — for one must elevate her from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> which take hold of her more intensely — in the aspect of <span class="hl-pink"><em>"raglehah yordos maves"</em> — "her feet descend to death"</span> [<em>Mishlei</em> 5:5] — and to elevate her through joy in the aspect mentioned above, until she rises to the aspect of <em>Keser</em>, in the aspect of <em>"ishah oleh imo"</em> — <em>"a woman ascends with him"</em> — so that the connection be drawn from the aspect of union and the totality of pursuit with restraint, etc., as above.</p>

      <p>The essential perfection is when one merits to ascend there in the aspect of <em>ratzo vashov</em>, until one merits to draw divine bounty from there — which is the aspect of the descent of divine bounty after prayer, as above. For sometimes one ascends and is included there for a brief moment, and is immediately expelled from there receiving nothing — and sometimes the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> then provoke him even more — for they are constantly lying in ambush for him, and when they see that he desires to flee from them and ascend to the lofty place mentioned above, they provoke him even more when he doesn't draw back a strong and durable impression [<em class="trans">rshimu</em>] that could enable him to stand against them.</p>

      <p>As is understood from the Torah-teaching <em>"Vayomer Boaz el Rus"</em> — see there <span class="xref">(§65)</span>. For the aspect mentioned above — of the attainment of the nine chambers — though it is an exceedingly lofty level attained only by the greatest and most select holy <em>tzadikim</em>, nevertheless even with ordinary people who draw themselves toward serving Hashem in truth — even with them it sometimes happens that there reaches them some illumination and divine spark flowing from there, from the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above. As is understood from the Torah-teaching <em>"Anochi"</em>, §4 in Likutay [Moharan Part] I, etc. — that even to ordinary people the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> is sometimes opened during their prayer.</p>

      <p>But to each person it reaches according to his world and level. For even in the world of <em>Asiyah</em> there is an aspect of sparkling from the nine chambers mentioned above. And even though even mere sparkling at any level is a very great merit — nonetheless the essential [goal] is when one merits to draw vitality and holy divine bounty from there so that one has the strength to sustain oneself thereafter through whatever befalls him, and to stand in the battle — for certainly thereafter when returning from there, the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> provoke him even more — like two people fighting each other, etc. — as is explained elsewhere. And one must strengthen oneself against them through the good impression [<em>rshimu</em>] remaining from the sparkling mentioned above — through which one merits always to be in His unity and oneness and the pleasantness of His closeness.</p>

      <p>And one can draw upon oneself <span class="hl-yellow">awe [<em class="trans">yirah</em>]</span> through this, to stand against those who provoke him — if he guards the memory [<em class="trans">zikaron</em>] well, to remember Him, may He be blessed, at every moment — after Hashem, may He be blessed, has already had mercy on him and illuminated to him some sparkling. As is explained in his holy words, of blessed memory — that one who has even a spark of Hashem, may He be blessed, sparkling to him — see there in §222 of Likutay [Moharan Part] I.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מַה שֶּׁחַיָּב לִתֵּן לְאִשְׁתּוֹ כְּתֻבָּה...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS YUD-ALEPH ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 11 — Why the <em>Kesuvah</em> Is Collected Only at Separation; the Mystery of Cohabitation and the Soul of the Convert</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>Returning to our subject: therefore <b>it is forbidden to cohabit with one's wife without a <em>kesuvah</em></b>, and the <em>kesuvah</em> was not given to be collected while both are alive and while she is with him — only after his death or after divorce. For it is necessary that the connection should not be, G-d forbid, like <span class="hl-pink">illicit cohabitation</span>, which is only for the moment to gratify one's desire, G-d forbid — but rather that the connection be a complete and enduring bond. For no union is ever wasted, G-d forbid — for even when it does not result in actual offspring, some souls are drawn from it: souls of <em>gerim</em> [converts], as is brought in the holy Zohar.</p>

      <p>Therefore one must give her a <em>kesuvah</em> — obligating himself to give her the divine bounty of wealth when she leaves him — to indicate that a residual impression [<em>rshimu</em>] from the union remains. For he drew the divine bounty of wealth from there — since the essential channel of divine bounty is through her specifically — through the formation of the light on its return in the aspect of the restrainer, as above. And this is the secret of what our Sages of blessed memory said: <em>"The reason for the <em>kesuvah</em> is so that divorcing her should not be easy in his eyes"</em> — namely as above — for the bond must be enduring and strong. And this is effected through the <em>kesuvah</em> by which he obligates himself that even when she leaves him, she shall not leave empty-handed — rather he is obligated to give her the divine bounty of wealth flowing from the totality of pursuit and restraint in <em>ratzo vashov</em>, whose channel of divine bounty is through her specifically.</p>

      <p>And therefore if he sends her away empty-handed, G-d forbid — <b>then his cohabitation [retroactively] was the cohabitation of <em class="trans">licentiousness</em></b> [<em class="trans">be'ilas zenus</em>] — for he demonstrates that he drew no divine bounty through her from above. Therefore he must give her a <em>kesuvah</em> when he sends her away — so that there remains with her from him the divine bounty of wealth drawn from the impression remaining from the union — since the essential channel of divine bounty is through her, as above — so that through this she can be saved from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> that want to take hold of her even more intensely — especially at the time of separation from her husband through death or divorce, when she remains alone. For her essential vitality and strength against them is through the divine bounty of wealth — which is the aspect of the <em>kesuvah</em> she receives from her husband, drawn from the aspect of the <em>rshimu</em>, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְנַחֲזֹר לְעִנְיָנֵנוּ, וְעַל-כֵּן אָסוּר לָדוּר עִם אִשְׁתּוֹ בְּלֹא כְּתֻבָּה...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS YUD-BEIS ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 12 — The Amount of the Biblical <em>Kesuvah</em>: Fifty Shekels / Fifty Gates of Understanding / Fifty Clasps</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And therefore <b>the amount of the Biblical <em>kesuvah</em> is fifty shekels of silver</b>, as derived from the verse: <em>"v'nasan la'avi hana'arah chamishim kesef"</em> — <em>"and he shall give the father of the girl fifty [shekels of] silver"</em> [<em>Devarim</em> 22:29]. For all attainments and all contemplations flow from the impression remaining from the nullification and inclusion in the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the <span class="hl-blue">fifty gates of understanding [<em>chamishim sha'aray binah</em>]</span> — for the fiftieth gate cannot be attained, and one needs to draw it through fifty gates until some impression from there is grasped in the mind.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>terumah</em> — which is <em>"tray mah"</em> — two from a hundred — as our Sages of blessed memory said — that is, one from fifty. For all the wealth mentioned above is essential through the <em>Kohen</em> who drew the blessing of intellect, as above — therefore he receives <em>terumah</em> — one from fifty. For he draws from there the aspect of fifty gates of understanding — and by giving the <em>Kohen</em> one from fifty of the grain's bounty, all the grain is blessed and holiness flows to it through the fifty gates mentioned above — so that through this the grain is proper for Israelite consumption, that one can know Him, may He be blessed, through eating this grain. For this is the essential purpose of all <em>mitzvos</em> connected to eating — especially bread — so that the food be sanctified, enabling one through this eating to draw vitality and holy knowledge to recognize Him, may He be blessed.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>"achuz echad min hachamishim"</em> — <em>"one grasped from the fifty"</em> — for when the light passes through the fifty gates, some impression from the sparkling mentioned above is then grasped and apprehended in the mind. And this is the aspect of the <span class="hl-green">fifty golden clasps</span> that joined the inner curtains — over the <em>Kodesh Kodashim</em> — to the outer curtains. For the essential attainment of the nine chambers mentioned above was in the <em>Kodesh Kodashim</em>, where the <em>Kohen Gadol</em> entered <em>"lifnai vlifnim"</em> [<em>into the innermost</em>] on Yom Kippur — and there he entered the place he entered and ascended to the place he ascended, in ultimate nullification before the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em>. This is the aspect of attaining the nine chambers, which he merited on the tenth day — Yom Kippur — after the Israelites had sanctified themselves and merited repentance during the nine preceding days from <em>Rosh Hashana</em> through Yom Kippur, corresponding to the nine chambers.</p>

      <p>And therefore there were fifty golden clasps joining the outer curtains with the inner curtains — for to draw the light of the impression from the inner curtains over the <em>Kodesh Kodashim</em>, where the essential nullification before the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> takes place, one must traverse fifty gates — the aspect of fifty gates of understanding. Corresponding to these are the fifty clasps joining the two curtains — for multiple ties are needed to connect and unify and bind the light of the impression to the mind, so that it remain tied and bound to the person so that he can remember himself at every moment before Him, may He be blessed. As is stated in <em>Tikkun Zohar</em>: <em>"When Shema Yisrael is called, they tie him in many ties of <em>tzitzis</em> and <em>tefillin</em>, etc."</em> — as above; understand well.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of the <b>fifty days of <em>Matan Torah</em></b> — the aspect of the <b>fifty years of <em>Yovel</em></b> [Jubilee]. For the essential purpose of <em>Matan Torah</em> was that all Israel merited attaining G-dliness — to know Him, may He be blessed — as it is written: <em>"panim b'fanim diber Hashem imachem"</em> — <em>"face to face did Hashem speak with you"</em> [<em>Devarim</em> 5:4] — the essential attainment flowed from the nullification mentioned above. Therefore one must prepare oneself during the <span class="hl-orange">forty-nine days of the <em>Omer</em></span> — to be able to receive the light of the impression on the fiftieth day specifically — for it cannot be received except through fifty gates, corresponding to which are fifty days. And this itself is the aspect of the fifty years of <em>Yovel</em> — for the Jubilee year is exceedingly sanctified, and its essential sanctity is on Yom Kippur — for then is the essential nullification before the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em>, as above. Therefore one must count until the fiftieth year, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְעַל-כֵּן שִׁעוּר כְּתֻבָּה דְּאוֹרָיְתָא הוּא חֲמִשִּׁים שֶׁקֶל כֶּסֶף...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS YUD-GIMEL ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 13 — The Exodus from Egypt as Paradigm; <em>Vachamishhim Alu</em></div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of <em class="trans">"vachamushhim alu vnay Yisrael me'eretz Mitzrayim"</em> — <em>"and the children of Israel went up from Egypt <em>vachamushhim</em>"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 13:18]. <span class="note">[The word <em>vachamushhim</em> is cognate to fifty, <em>chamishim</em>; Reb Nosson reads it as: armed with the fifty-gate consciousness.]</span></p>

      <p>For the land of Egypt [<em>Eretz Mitzrayim</em>] is the aspect of the place of the <em>sitra achara</em> — the aspect of the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>. Israel had to be in exile there in order to refine holiness from there, through the power of the great <em>tzadikim</em> — for specifically by descending there and standing in the battle and refining holiness from there, they ascended through great ascents, ascent after ascent, until they merited attainment of the nine chambers mentioned above — from which the receiving of the Torah flowed. This is the aspect of what was said to Yaakov: <em>"Anochi ered imcha mitzraymah v'anochi a'alcha gam aloh"</em> — <em>"I shall descend with you to Egypt, and I shall also bring you up, fully up"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 46:4] — that specifically by descending to Egypt, the place of the <em>klippos</em> — <em>"and I shall fully bring you up"</em> — ascending ascent after ascent until meriting the attainment mentioned above.</p>

      <p>And <em>"lo nacham Elokim derech eretz Plishtim ki karov hu"</em> — <em>"G-d did not lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines, for it was near"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 13:17] — that He did not permit them to ascend and be included there immediately, before the rectification of the restrainer mentioned above was established. For then no good impression would have remained with them and they would have had no power to stand in the battle that provokes even more intensely when returning from nullification, as above. <em>"Lo nacham"</em> [<em>did not guide them</em>] — the word <em>Plishtim</em> implies something opened and cleared [<em>mefulash</em>] — that He did not want to allow them the cleared path where the light would be revealed to them immediately without many circuits and delays. <em>"Ki karov hu"</em> — <em>"for it was near"</em> — and when the light would be revealed to them immediately, no impression would remain, and they could not stand in the battle, as above.</p>

      <p>And this: <em>"ki amar Elokim, pen yinachem ha'am bir'osam milchamah v'shavu mitzraymah"</em> — <em>"for G-d said: lest the people regret when they see battle and return to Egypt"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 13:17] — as above. And therefore: <em>"vayasev Elokim es ha'am"</em> — <em>"G-d led the people around"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 13:18] — He circuited them and delayed them through many circuits and delays so that through this the rectification of the restrainer would be established — and then they could receive the light of the impression through fifty gates — which is the aspect of <em>"vachamushhim alu vnay Yisrael me'eretz Mitzrayim"</em>, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה בְּחִינַת וַחֲמֻשִׁים עָלוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS YUD-DALET ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 14 — Practical Guidance: Joy in Every <em>Mitzvah</em>; Holding the Spark</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And all this transpires for every person who wishes to draw close to Him, may He be blessed. The essential foundation is that one must <span class="hl-yellow">strengthen himself greatly to always be in joy</span> and to perform <em>mitzvos</em> with great joy — and the more he knows his distance, the more he must strengthen himself to be joyful. Especially at the moment of performing some <em>mitzvah</em>, for he too has merited to perform His <em>mitzvos</em> — since the light of each and every <em>mitzvah</em> no worlds can receive except the holy Israelite nation who merit to perform them in this world. And then he will merit to ascend higher and higher until, through Hashem's mercy, he merits to be included in the aspect of the nine chambers as above, according to his level.</p>

      <p>This is the aspect of the divine sparkling that is sometimes drawn upon each person — according to what each one knows in his own soul — about which it is impossible to speak at all. And then <b>the essential thing is to strengthen himself not to let the sparkling completely pass from him, G-d forbid</b> — but rather that a good impression [<em>rshimu</em>] should remain. And he should see to bind the impression to himself through many strong and enduring bonds — namely, not to allow the memory of the sparkling to pass from his mind — and through this he will remember himself at every moment before Him, may He be blessed, so that he can stand in the battle that intensifies greatly when the spirit of Hashem begins to stir him and His G-dliness sparkles to him, as above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְכָל זֶה עוֹבֵר עַל כָּל אָדָם הָרוֹצֶה לְהִתְקָרֵב אֵלָיו יִתְבָּרַךְ...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS TES-VAV ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 15 — The Song of Songs as Allegory; "The Voice of My Beloved Knocks"</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And all this is well alluded to in the verses of <em>Shir haShirim</em> [Song of Songs], which in its entirety speaks of the pleasantness of clinging to His G-dliness. And this is: <em>"kol dodi dofek pischi li"</em> — <em>"The voice of my beloved knocks — open to me"</em> [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 5:2] — some sparkling reaches him. And when one does not arouse oneself to draw close to Him as needed — the aspect of: <em>"pashatti es kutoness, eichachah elbashenah"</em> — <em>"I have taken off my robe, how shall I put it on again?"</em> — one is lazy and lethargic and does not truly arouse oneself to His service — then <em>"dodi shalach yado min hachor"</em> — <em>"my beloved stretched forth his hand through the hole"</em> [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 5:4] — alludes that Hashem begins to arouse him through suffering, G-d forbid — as Rashi explains there, referencing the communal narrative of Israel against whom He sent the nations — Plishtim, etc. And then: <em>"pasachti ani l'dodi v'dodi chamak avar"</em> — <em>"I opened to my beloved but my beloved had turned and was gone"</em> [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 5:6] — this is the aspect above that sometimes when a person does not strengthen himself sufficiently, then <em>"v'dodi chamak avar bikashtihu v'lo m'tzasihu"</em> — His light, may He be blessed, is hidden from him and he cannot find Him even though in prior days His light sparkled to him.</p>

      <p>And then it says: <em>"mtz'uni hashomrim hassovevim ba'ir"</em> — <em>"the watchmen who go about the city found me"</em> [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 5:7] — who are the gatekeepers flowing from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>. <em>"Hikuni f'tza'uni"</em> — <em>"they struck me, they wounded me"</em> — for then they provoke him more intensely, as above. Therefore every person must strengthen himself greatly to hold fast to the sparkling mentioned above and to bind it in his mind and thought with strong bonds so it not be forgotten — until he merits through this to arrive at the ultimate good, in the aspect of:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">אֲחַזְתִּיו וְלֹא אַרְפֶּנּוּ עַד שֶׁהֲבֵיאתִיו אֶל בֵּית אִמִּי</span><br>"I held him and would not let him go, until I brought him into my mother's house" [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 3:4]</span>

      <p>— to hold it without letting go until bringing it to the aspect of the Holy Temple — which is the aspect of <em>"beis imi"</em> — as Rashi explains. That is, the aspect of attaining true <em>da'as</em> [knowledge/intimacy with G-d] called the Holy Temple, as our Sages of blessed memory said: <em>"Whoever has <em>da'as</em> is as if the Holy Temple was built in his days."</em> As is cited in the words of our Sages of blessed memory many times. <em>Amen</em>, may it be His will.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְכָל זֶה מְרֻמָּז הֵיטֵב בִּפְסוּקֵי שִׁיר הַשִּׁירִים...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════ OIS TES-ZAYIN / TES-CHES / TES-TES ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="ois-header">§ 16 — The Exodus with Great Wealth; Moshe's Turning This Way and That</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And therefore <b>they left Egypt with great wealth</b>, as He promised Avraham our father, peace be upon him: <em>"v'acharay chen yetzeu birechush gadol"</em> — <em>"and afterward they shall go out with great wealth"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 15:14] — for they merited to draw down the divine bounty of wealth from the attainments mentioned above that they merited through having refined holiness from the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> — which is the aspect of the Exodus from Egypt, as above.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ois-header">§ 17 — Moshe Turning This Way and That / Fifty Letters of <em>Shema</em></div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is the aspect of: <em>"vayifen ko vacoh vayar ki ayn ish"</em> — <em>"and he turned this way and that and saw there was no man"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 2:12]. <em>"Vayifen ko vacoh"</em> — it is stated in <em>Tikkun Zohar</em> that these are the aspect of the <em>fifty letters of the Shema</em> — namely the aspect above: when one is included in His unity in <em>Shema Yisrael</em>, one must draw the light of the impression from there through fifty gates — the aspect of the fifty letters of <em>Shema</em>.</p>

      <p>And <em>"vayar ki ayn ish"</em> — for the one who merits to nullify himself and be included in the aspect of the nine chambers mentioned above must nullify himself in ultimate nullification — as if he does not exist in the world — the aspect of <em>"vayar ki ayn ish"</em>, for he has nullified himself entirely, in the aspect of: <em>"v'chol adam lo yihyeh b'ohel mo'ed b'vo'o"</em> — <em>"and no man shall be in the tent of meeting when he enters"</em> [<em>Vayikra</em> 16:17].</p>

      <p>And then <em>"vayach es haMitzri"</em> — <em>"he struck the Egyptian"</em> — which is the <em>sitra achara</em>, the aspect of <em>heichalei hatemuros</em>. For then he merited to strike and subdue and shatter the <em>sitra achara</em> entirely — having now nullified himself in ultimate nullification and merited to draw the light from there through fifty gates of understanding, the fifty letters of <em>Shema</em>, as above.</p>


    </div>

    <div class="ois-header">§ 18 — The Paroches [Curtain]; Fifty Golden Clasps</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is: <em>"v'nasata es haparoches tachas haKrasim"</em> — <em>"and you shall place the curtain below the clasps"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 26:33]. For the <em>paroches</em> [curtain] between the <em>Kodesh Kodashim</em> and the <em>Ohel Mo'ed</em> is the aspect of the <em>prisa</em> [veil] mentioned in the passage of the holy Zohar brought in the Torah-teaching above — see there — which is the aspect of the arranger and settler, the aspect of the restrainer as above, through which comes the essential attainment of the nine chambers that are attained in the <em>Kodesh Kodashim</em>, as above. And therefore there were the fifty golden clasps directed over the <em>paroches</em> placed beneath them — for from there flows the impression through fifty gates, as above.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ois-header">§ 19 — Avraham at the Oaks of Mamre; Sitting at the Tent Entrance; Running to Meet the Angels</div>
    <div class="english-block">
      <p>And this is: <em>"vayera elav Hashem b'elonei Mamre v'hu yoshev pesach ha'ohel k'chom hayom"</em> — <em>"And Hashem appeared to him in the oaks of Mamre, and he was sitting at the entrance of the tent in the heat of the day"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:1]. <em>"Vayera elav Hashem"</em> — this is the aspect of divine revelation that one merits through attainment of the nine chambers from which flows all attainment and revelation, as above. And this cannot be merited except by entering the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> and refining holiness from there, as explained in the Torah-teaching regarding <em>"mi yeimar"</em>.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>"b'elonei Mamre"</em> — <em>"Mamre"</em> is the language of exchange [<em>temurah</em>] — the language of <em>"v'im hamayr yemirenhu"</em> [<em>"and if he substitutes it"</em>]. And <em>"b'elonei Mamre"</em> is the aspect of the two trees — the <em>ilan d'chayay</em> [tree of life] and the <em>ilan d'mosa</em> [tree of death] — where the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> take hold, seeking to exchange and substitute them to distance the person, G-d forbid, from the tree of life to the opposite, G-d forbid. And specifically through them Hashem was revealed to him — until he merited to refine them, to separate good from evil and to elevate holiness from there in the aspects mentioned above — until he merited the revelation of G-dliness, the aspect of <em>"vayera elav Hashem"</em>. For he merited to ascend through the ascents mentioned above until meriting attainment of the nine chambers from which flows all revelation, as above.</p>

      <p>And what our Sages of blessed memory said — that <em>Mamre</em> gave him counsel regarding the circumcision — this is the aspect of <em>"u'far'oh hikriv"</em> [<em>"and Pharaoh drew near"</em>] — that he drew Israel close to their Father in Heaven. For one who is mindful of his true eternal life — every time he sees the <em>sitra achara</em> (<em>heichalei hatemuros</em>) overpowering and spreading and expanding more and more — equally he strengthens and exerts and hastens himself more to draw close to Hashem, because he sees that they want to reject him entirely, G-d forbid. And this is the aspect of: distance that is the ultimate closeness; descent that is the ultimate ascent. And this is the aspect of: <em>"he gave him counsel regarding circumcision"</em> — namely to circumcise the foreskin of his heart. For specifically through the aspect of <em>Mamre</em> — the aspect of <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> that overpowered and spread over him so greatly — through this specifically he counseled himself to circumcise his heart, the aspect of <em>"u'far'oh hikriv"</em>, as above.</p>

      <p>And <em>"v'hu yoshev pesach ha'ohel k'chom hayom"</em> — <em>"and he was sitting at the entrance of the tent in the heat of the day."</em> <em>"Yeshivah"</em> [sitting] implies delay for a long time — as in <em>"vateshevu b'Kadesh yamim rabbim"</em> [<em>"and you settled in Kadesh for many days"</em>] — that he merited this revelation because he sat and waited and was delayed many days at the entrance of the tent — which is the entrance of holiness — the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>, which is the first level through which one must ascend until arriving at the attainment mentioned above, which is called entrance and gateway, as is known. The aspect of: <em>"zeh hasha'ar laHashem"</em> — <em>"this is the gate of Hashem"</em>, etc.</p>

      <p>But when one wants to enter there, the <em>sitra achara</em> — the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em> — overpowers and spreads greatly against him. And the closer one is to the entrance, the more intensely they overpower and spread against him — until many who were already at the entrance turned back, G-d have mercy, since they didn't know they were already at the entrance — or they spread against him so intensely that it was hard for him to break them. As is explained from his holy words <span class="xref">(Likutay Moharan II, §51)</span>. But <b>he sat and was delayed at the entrance of the tent</b>. <em>"K'chom hayom"</em> — <em>"in the heat of the day"</em> — this is the aspect of the strengthening heat of the <em>yetzer hara</em>. Regarding this it says:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">אֵיכָה תִרְעֶה אֵיכָה תַּרְבִּיץ בַּצָּהֳרָיִם</span><br>"How will you pasture? How will you make them rest at noon?" [<em>Shir haShirim</em> 1:7]</span>

      <p>— for then it is a difficult time for the flock — as Rashi explains there — for noon is the aspect of <em>"chom hayom"</em> — the heat of the day — the aspect of the heat of the <em>yetzer hara</em>, which is then a difficult time for the holy flock that the <em>tzadik</em> shepherds — those who wish to approach holiness — and many distanced themselves through this, G-d have mercy. As it is written: <em>"ad sheyafuach hayom"</em> — <em>"until the day cools"</em> — as Rashi explains there: that Israel was closely bound to Hashem with greatness and honor until <em>"the day cooled"</em> — the heat of the day overpowered — and through this the Temple was destroyed.</p>

      <p>But one who does not want to deceive himself and truly contemplates his eternal purpose — he will not turn back under any circumstance whatsoever. Rather he <b>sits and waits and delays at the entrance</b> as many days as will be — and even when they let him enter the entrance and the heat of the day scorches him intensely, he still does not abandon his place but sits and delays at the tent entrance of the <em>tzadikim</em> and righteous until he is shown mercy from Heaven. The aspect of: <em>"v'hu yoshev pesach ha'ohel k'chom hayom"</em>, as above.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of: <em>"v'Yehoshua bin Nun na'ar lo yamish mitoch ha'ohel"</em> — <em>"and Yehoshua bin Nun, a youth, did not depart from within the tent"</em> [<em>Shemos</em> 33:11]. Yehoshua is the aspect of the disciple of the true <em>tzadik</em> who is called Moshe — as our master, teacher, and <em>rebbe</em>, of blessed memory, wrote: that wherever there is a <em>rebbe</em> and student, they are the aspects of Moshe and Yehoshua and the <em>Ohel Mo'ed</em>. And for this reason the student is called Yehoshua — from the name <em>"Yah yoshia'cha"</em> [<em>"G-d will save you"</em>] — as our Sages of blessed memory expounded — that all his life and hope is on the power of his <em>rebbe</em> the <em>tzadik</em> who continually prays for him: <em>"Yah yoshia'cha"</em> — may Hashem save him from the counsel of the <em>sitra achara</em> that overpowers and spreads over him at every time.</p>

      <p>And this: <em>"v'Yehoshua bin Nun na'ar"</em> — even when he was in the aspect of a youth — in the aspect of youthful deeds — nevertheless <em>"lo yamish mitoch ha'ohel"</em> — for nevertheless he stood at the entrance for a long time until he pressed himself inside the tent and did not move from within it, as above.</p>

      <p>And this is: <em>"vayisa eynav vayar v'hinay shloshah anashim nitzavim alav"</em> — <em>"and he lifted his eyes and saw, and behold three men were standing over him"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:2]. <em>"Shloshah"</em> [three] — this is the aspect of the elevation of holiness mentioned above which is always in threes — for <em>Malchus</em> clothes <em>Netzach, Hod, Yesod</em> — which are three attributes — and <em>Netzach, Hod, Yesod</em> clothe <em>Chesed, Gevurah, Tiferes</em>, and <em>Chesed, Gevurah, Tiferes</em> clothe <em>Chochma, Binah, Da'as</em>, etc., as explained in the Torah-teaching mentioned above. And this is the aspect of three men standing over him — for they stand over him and above him, for he must ascend to them — since at every level there stand the three aspects which are the aspect of the three men of the higher level, all of which are composed of three upon three, as above. And this is the threefold holiness [<em>kedushshah meshuleshes</em>] — for all ascent of holiness is in threes, as above.</p>

      <p>And this is: <em>"Brich Rachmana d'yahiv lan Oraisa tlis'ah al yad tlis'ah b'yom tlis'ah"</em> — <em>"Blessed is the Merciful One Who gave us the Torah, which is threefold, through a thirdborn, on the third day"</em> [<em>Shabbos</em> 88a] — for all aspects of the elevation of holiness that one merits through the Torah are in the threefold structure, as above.</p>

      <p>And this: <em>"vayar vayaratz likrasam"</em> — <em>"and he saw and he ran to meet them"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:2]. <em>"Vayaratz"</em> [he ran] — this is the aspect of <b>alacrity and joy</b> — for alacrity is the aspect of joy, as is understood in the Torah-teaching <em>"Arichas Apayim"</em> [<em>Longanimity</em>] <span class="xref">(§155 in Likutay I)</span>. And as our Sages of blessed memory said: <em>"It is a <em>mitzvah</em> to run to the synagogue and to a matter of <em>mitzvah</em>"</em> — as it says:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">שָׂמַחְתִּי בְּאֹמְרִים לִי בֵּית ה' נֵלֵךְ</span><br>"I rejoiced when they said to me: Let us go to the house of Hashem" [<em>Tehillim</em> 122:1].</span>

      <p>For one who truly gazes at his purpose — certainly when the opportunity comes to go to the synagogue or to a matter of <em>mitzvah</em>, he runs with great joy and alacrity — for this alone is his life and hope for eternity, and outside of this everything is vanity of vanities. For nothing remains of anything — not of wealth, not from the pain of poverty and want, not from any matter of desire, honor, envy, hatred, and resentment — as it is written: <em>"ki lo b'moso yikach hakol"</em> — <em>"for in his death he cannot take anything"</em>, etc. And it is written:</p>

      <span class="verse-subtitle"><span class="hebrew-inline">גַּם אַהֲבָתָם גַּם קִנְאָתָם גַּם שִׂנְאָתָם כְּבָר אָבָדָה</span><br>"Their love, their envy, and their hatred — all have already perished" [<em>Koheles</em> 9:6].</span>

      <p>Only what one seizes at each moment — some good thing: to go to the synagogue or house of study, or to perform some <em>mitzvah</em> — this is all that remains. Therefore certainly every person is obligated to run with great alacrity and joy to a matter of <em>mitzvah</em>. And the more he knows he is distant from Hashem — the more he is obligated to rejoice in performing the <em>mitzvah</em>, since he too, who is so distant, also merits to perform a <em>mitzvah</em>.</p>

      <p>And this is the aspect of <em>"vayar"</em> — Rashi explains: <em>"he understood"</em> — that he understood well and truly gazed at his purpose. And through this: <em>"vayaratz likrasam"</em> — this is the aspect of the joy of the <em>mitzvah</em>, through which comes the essential elevation of holiness from the <em>klippos</em> until meriting the ascents mentioned above, until arriving at the attainment mentioned above.</p>

      <p>And this: <em>"vayaratz likrasam mi'pesach ha'ohel"</em> — <em>"he ran to meet them from the entrance of the tent"</em> — this is the aspect of the beginning of the elevation of holiness, which is the aspect of <em>pesach</em> [entrance], the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>, as above. <em>"Vayishtachu artzah"</em> — <em>"and he bowed to the ground"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:2] — this is the aspect of nullification and inclusion in the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> — for all prostrations are the aspect of nullification — one falls to the ground and prostrates, extending hands and feet in nullification of all sensations, because of the greatness of the pristine light revealed to him. This is the aspect of the attainment of the nine chambers — the aspect of attainment of the light of the <em>Ein Sof</em> in the mode of <em>matay velo matay</em>, where the essential prostration in the aspect of nullification occurs, as above.</p>

      <p>That is: through joy — which is the aspect of <em>"vayaratz likrasam"</em> — one merited the attainment of the pristine lights mentioned above, where the prostration [<em>hishtachaviyah</em>] in the aspect of nullification occurs, as above.</p>

      <p>And this is: <em>"vayomer, Adonai, im na matzasi chen b'eynecha al na ta'avor me'al avdecha"</em> — <em>"and he said: My Lord, if I have found favor in Your eyes, please do not pass from your servant"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:3] — he beseeched Hashem that He not pass from him — that the revelation not pass from him until a good impression remains with him, as above — for one must strive greatly that the revelation not quickly pass from him until a good impression remains with which one can sustain oneself always. And this is what Avraham beseeched of Hashem who was revealed to him then: <em>"al na ta'avor me'al avdecha."</em></p>

      <p>And this: <em>"yukach na m'at mayim"</em> — <em>"please let a little water be taken"</em> [<em>Bereishis</em> 18:4] — this is an allusion to the drawing down of divine bounty — he beseeched that the revelation not pass until drawing divine bounty from there, as above — which is the aspect of the descent of divine bounty after prayer, as above.</p>

      <p class="source-attr">Halachah 5 of Hilchos Pirya viRivya, Halachah 4.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hebrew-block" dir="rtl" style="line-height:2; font-size:1.05rem; text-align:right;">
      <p>וְזֶה, "וַיֵּרָא אֵלָיו ה' בְּאֵלֹנֵי מַמְרֵא..."</p>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider">

    <!-- ═══════════════════ TRANSLATOR'S SUMMARY ═══════════════════ -->
    <div class="summary-box">
      <h3>Translator's Summary — Eishus §4</h3>

      <p>This is one of the most architecturally elaborate sections in <em>Likutay Halachos</em>. Reb Nosson uses the halachic topic of intermarriage between <em>Kohanim</em>, <em>Leviim</em>, and <em>Yisraelim</em> as a springboard to expound a comprehensive spiritual cosmology, all drawing on Rebbe Nachman's Torah <em>"Emtza'isa d'Alma"</em> (Likutay Moharan I, §24).</p>

      <br>
      <p><strong style="color:#e8c84b;">The Central Mechanism:</strong></p>

      <div class="flowchart">
        <div class="flow-node highlight">Joy in <em>Mitzvos</em> → Elevates holiness from <em>Klippos</em> (incense / <em>ketores</em>)</div>
        <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="flow-node">Ascent through the Spiritual Worlds → Blessing of Intellect (<em>Birkas haSeichel</em>)</div>
        <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="flow-node highlight">Attainment of 9 Chambers (<em>Heichalos</em>) = Light of <em>Ein Sof</em> — in mode of <em>matay velo matay</em> (reaching yet not reaching)</div>
        <div class="flow-arrow">↓ ↕</div>
        <div class="flow-node">Dual forces: PURSUIT (<em>redifahs hamachshavah</em>) + RESTRAINER (<em>hame'akev / Keser</em>)</div>
        <div class="flow-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="flow-node"><em>Ratzo vaShov</em> (Running &amp; Returning) → Descent of Divine Bounty (<em>shefa</em>) = Wealth; <em>Kesuvah</em></div>
      </div>

      <br>
      <p><strong style="color:#e8c84b;">The Triple Correspondence:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kohen</strong> = Pursuit of intellect-lights → Sacrifices + <em>Birkas Kohanim</em></li>
        <li><strong>Levi</strong> = The Restrainer (<em>Keser</em>) → Song from the Left Side</li>
        <li><strong>Yisrael</strong> = Joy of Torah and <em>Mitzvos</em> → Standing at the Ma'amad</li>
        <li><strong>Husband</strong> = Pursuit; <strong>Wife</strong> = Restrainer / <em>Keser</em> — <em>"Eshes chayil ateres ba'alah"</em></li>
      </ul>

      <br>
      <p><strong style="color:#e8c84b;">Key Halachic Derivations:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Child follows father: intellect-light flows through the male (pursuit)</li>
        <li>Child follows deficient parent: sin activates the <em>heichalei hatemuros</em></li>
        <li>Betrothal with money (<em>kesef</em>): money's root is in <em>Keser</em> — the same root as the woman</li>
        <li><em>Kesuvah</em> = 50 shekels = 50 Gates of Understanding = impression (<em>rshimu</em>) preserved from union</li>
        <li><em>Ketores</em> brings wealth: it elevates the worlds, drawing bounty through the restrainer</li>
        <li><em>Kohen</em> must be married: the woman = the restrainer; without it, dangerous imbalanced ascent (Nadav &amp; Avihu)</li>
      </ul>

      <br>
      <p><strong style="color:#e8c84b;">Historical Paradigms woven in:</strong> The Golden Calf (sin of investigating the <em>Ein Sof</em>) — rectified by the Tabernacle • Israel in Egypt (exile as extraction of sparks) • Exodus with 50 gates • <em>Shema Yisrael</em>'s 50 letters • Avraham at Mamre (sitting at the tent entrance despite the heat) • Moshe turning this way and that (50 letters of Shema) • Yehoshua not departing from the tent • Shir haShirim as allegory of the soul's pursuit of G-d.</p>
    </div>

